  "id": "attenuated-psychotic-symptoms",
  "term": "attenuated psychotic symptoms",
  "definition": "Attenuated psychotic symptoms are reduced-intensity psychotic-like experiences that emerge in people considered at ultra-high risk for psychosis. In this context, they are used as part of identifying increased risk and often occur alongside worsening day-to-day functioning.",
